      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#hammond-1819\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EHammond 1819\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E;",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003E\u003Ci\u003ETreacle beer\u003C/i\u003E\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nPut a gallon of boiling water to two pounds of treacle, mix them well, add twelve quarts of cold water and half a pint of yeast, put it into a cask, cover it close, and in three days it will be fit to drink. If made in large quantities or designed to keep, put in some malt and hops, and when the fermentation is over, stop it up close.\u003Cbr\u003E"
